@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: what the two guiding wizards, `proveo run` and `proveo init`, gain from one step model, a tree picker, sbx's control vocabulary and a prompt kit
' status: proposed 2026-11-10, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: cmd/proveo/main.go (pickProject, fuzzyPickProject, pickProjectNumbered)
' would touch: cmd/proveo/running.go, cmd/proveo/schedule.go, cmd/proveo-dev/maintain.go (the other pickers)
' would touch: internal/run/run.go (resolveWorkspace, the scope gate, the page loop)
' would touch: internal/run/choices.go (the scope fact, the on-enter region)
' would touch: internal/choiceui/** (Form.hint, Step, leave, the modals, a tree, a button row)
' would touch: cmd/proveo/init.go (runInitSteps, the apply steps, the prompt kit)
' would touch: cmd/proveo/init_tui.go, init_credentials.go, init_operator.go, init_github_access.go
' would touch: internal/sbx/install.go or a sibling (the starship and font installers)
' would touch: internal/shell/shell.go, cmd/proveo/uninstall.go
'   the ORDER this is delivered in .. _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml
'   the wireframes, navigable ....... https://claude.ai/artifact/LBwgvN5Gxpux5edZR3XEj6
'   the vocabulary it borrows ....... _spec/_experiments/sbx-tui-observed.puml
'   the live list and the prompt .... _spec/_plans/tui-responsiveness.puml (P2, P3, P4)
'   the form these pages are ........ _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml
'   how a short terminal is handled . _spec/internal/choiceui/viewport.puml
'   init's three screens today ...... _spec/cmd/proveo/init-sbx-bootstrap.puml
'   the credential page ............. _spec/cmd/proveo/init-credential-wireframe.puml
'   the headless rule ............... _spec/_plans/tui-style-deferred-surfaces.puml (surface B)
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE TWO WIZARDS ARE TODAY (MEASURED BY READING, 2026-11-10) ───────
' `proveo run`
'   scope     fuzzyPickProject (cmd/proveo/main.go:420) hands go-fuzzyfinder a
'             flat list: "<repo root>", then every workspace.Project.Path, under
'             a "scope> " prompt. Abort, a finder error and the root all return
'             "". Nothing marks the root as the default. The choice cannot be
'             revisited: the finder is a different program from the form.
'             internal/run/run.go:130 calls the picker only on a terminal, so
'             pickProjectNumbered ("0) <repo root>", "scope [0]:") is reached
'             by tests only. A monorepo run with no terminal keeps the root
'             silently.
'             The scope is picked after the manifest and sandbox readiness
'             (run.go:67, :71, :132) and before the form (run.go:83).
'   options   one lone choiceui.Form, "confirm or change this run". Its Step is
'             zero, so the key line carries no page and no way back.
'             MEASURED: a `Step{2, 2}` form already draws "page 2/2 … shift+tab
'             back", so a second page costs choiceui nothing.
'   confirm   five typed y/N modals share readModal: ConfirmSandboxUpgrade and
'             ConfirmUnansweredRemoval (blocked_run.go), ConfirmSandboxClose,
'             ConfirmFetchPushed and ConfirmOversizedModel.
'   start     a stream; a line prints when a step ends.
'   finish    a stream; see tui-responsiveness.puml C1 to C3.
'   pickers   go-fuzzyfinder has three call sites in three files: the scope
'             (main.go:426), the run and attach list (running.go:26), and
'             proveo-dev's multi-select (maintain.go:106, FindMulti with tab).
' `proveo init`
'   three numbered pages — setup, credentials, operator — with page n/3 and
'   shift+tab back (init-sbx-bootstrap.puml, DECISION 2026-11-08). Two more
'   forms open, unnumbered, inside setup's apply (init_github_access.go:44,
'   :142). Enter on setup runs the install and every "now" action.
'   initHeader lists only the prereqs that FAILED; passing ones print in the
'   stream (init.go:226-227). There is no virtualisation prereq
'   (internal/sbx/install.go:326-341): that check is `sbx diagnose`, which runs
'   after the install (init.go:583).
'   Esc means THREE things: an error on setup (init_tui.go:112-114), a skip on
'   credentials (init_credentials.go:422-425), a clean end on operator
'   (init_operator.go:68-70). Ctrl+C shares all three.
'   The post-install installs sbx and nothing for the prompt.
'
' ── THE PROPOSALS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   W1  THE FOLDER PICKER IS A TREE. The repo root is the first row. It carries
'       a "default" chip and the cursor starts on it, so Enter alone keeps
'       today's answer. Folders derive from each Project.Path. ←/→ fold a
'       folder. "/" narrows the tree, and the root stays visible while it does.
'       One line under the tree always says where Enter starts the agent.
'       Cancel becomes distinct from the root.
'       NOT a per-project Tool column: internal/workspace/discover.go gives
'       every project in a repo the same Tool.
'       The page's Enter word is not "accept": e2e's acceptChoicePrompt waits
'       for "enter accept" and would press Enter on the scope page.
'   W2  ONE STEP MODEL FOR BOTH WIZARDS. The scope page becomes page 1 of
'       `proveo run` and the form page 2, through the Step{At, Of} init already
'       uses. resolveWorkspace splits into detect-once and apply-scope, so a
'       step back re-runs no detection. A chip top-right names the page
'       ("scope · 1/2"), as sbx's create wizard does ("1/2").
'       FIRST: one scope-gate predicate that also refuses under --yes and
'       PROVEO_SCHEDULE.
'       [Inference] A scheduled run in a monorepo directory opens the picker
'       and waits today; this rests on reading the gate, not on a run.
'   W3  TWO-TONE KEY HINTS. The key is bold and bright, its word is grey (sbx's
'       footer). Form.hint keeps its KEEP ranks and its plain projection, which
'       tests and e2e read.
'   W4  ONE BACK KEY, ONE MEANING PER KEY (D5, DECIDED). Esc steps back one
'       page and closes the wizard from page 1. Ctrl+C quits after a confirm.
'       Enter moves forward. shift+tab leaves the key line. Two new outcomes,
'       Skipped and Quit, replace the three meanings of Esc.
'       SKIP IS A FOCUSABLE BUTTON (D10, DECIDED). The first draft's `s` types
'       into the focused field (MEASURED): the credentials page opens on a
'       field and the operator page is one field.
'   W5  THE FORM SAYS WHAT ENTER WILL RUN. An "on enter" region lists the
'       actions in order: the sandbox name and clone mode for `run`; the install
'       and every "now" action for `init`. The count FOLLOWS the literal
'       "enter accept" in the key line; it never replaces it.
'   W6  A LIVE STEP LIST FOR EVERY PHASE THAT RUNS THINGS. Start, init's apply
'       and teardown share one renderer. A step that hands the terminal to
'       another program (`sbx login`) ends the list's Program and starts a new
'       one after it; five of init's apply steps do.
'   W7  INIT OPENS ON EVERY CHECK. The install prereqs, each with its mark, and
'       every `sbx diagnose` row when sbx is already installed.
'       On a fresh macOS host the page holds one row.
'   W8  INIT CLOSES ON THE RESULT. What is ready, what was answered "later"
'       with the command that does it, and the next command to type. It reads an
'       accumulated record of what ran, so a sign-in done before a step back
'       still counts as done.
'   W9  CONFIRMATIONS ARE BUTTON ROWS WITH A SAFE DEFAULT. The safe answer is
'       selected and carries ↵. A destructive answer shows its key as a bold
'       red letter inside the word (sbx's mnemonic). The first user is the
'       wizard's own Ctrl+C quit confirm, which destroys nothing. The five
'       typed y/N modals follow: destroying takes two keys, and Enter alone
'       never does (D7, DECIDED).
'   W10 THE PROMPT SEGMENT CLOSES `run`. tui-responsiveness D4.
'   W11 THE PROMPT KIT RIDES ALONG WITH sbx (D13, D14 — DECIDED). The setup
'       page gains one row, "prompt", now or later. Its apply steps:
'         starship  install the pinned release when `starship` is not on PATH
'         font      download FiraCode Nerd Font when the host has NO Nerd Font
'                   at install time
'         shell     add the `starship init` line to the detected shell's rc,
'                   unless one is there
'         segment   add a marked `[custom.proveo]` block to starship.toml
'       Then one page asks what the terminal draws: it shows a Nerd glyph and
'       offers "icon" or "empty box".
'         icon  proveo seeds starship's `nerd-font-symbols` preset
'         box   proveo seeds `no-nerd-font`, and prints the font setting for
'               the terminal in use
'       A preset is seeded only when init creates starship.toml. An existing
'       file gains the marked block and nothing else.
'       With --yes or no terminal: the same installs, the `no-nerd-font`
'       preset, no question.
'       [Inference] "The host has a Nerd Font" means a font file whose name
'       holds "NerdFont" or "Nerd Font" under the user and system font
'       directories. MEASURED on this host: that scan finds 18 FiraCode files
'       in ~/Library/Fonts. The Linux and Windows directories were not checked.
'       Turning starship on replaces the operator's whole prompt. The row's
'       help line says so.
'
' ── WHAT IS NOT BORROWED FROM sbx ──────────────────────────────────────────
' Its panels, cards and dashboard: proveo has no long-lived screen. Its
' centred dialogs over a dimmed dashboard: proveo's pages are full-screen
' forms and stay so. Its per-panel key reuse (`r` removes on the left and
' refreshes on the right): one key keeps one meaning across a proveo wizard.
'
' ── THE HEADLESS RULE STILL HOLDS ──────────────────────────────────────────
' Every page keeps a rendering with no terminal. Today: no scope picker without
' a TTY, with PROVEO_WIZARD off, with --print or with --scope; the form is
' skipped unless promptable and not --yes; confirmations decline unless headed;
' each init page prints one note and returns.
' The form's "resolved values" rendering does not exist yet. It is new work.
' tui-style-deferred-surfaces: "a form cannot be the only rendering".
'
' ── WHAT D5 CHANGES IN THE TESTS (COUNTED) ─────────────────────────────────
'   "shift+tab back"      7 string assertions: 3 in e2e, 4 in unit tests
'   the back key itself   3 e2e BTab sends, 4 unit backtab cases
'   "esc cancel"          1 unit assertion, plus 1 on "esc cancels"
'   Escape as skip/finish 6 e2e sends, in init_steps_test.go and
'                         init_github_access_test.go
'   "page n/3"            19 e2e literals, 3 unit
'   "enter accept"        stays the e2e anchor (e2e/instrument_test.go:180)
' One slice first routes the e2e waits and keys through four helpers, so each
' later change edits one helper.
'
' ── DECISIONS (2026-11-10) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   D5  the back key. DECIDED — the Executor: "Adopt sbx: esc back, ^c quit".
'       The recommendation was to keep shift+tab.
'   D3  the stack (tui-responsiveness.puml). DECIDED — the Executor: "Port
'       everything to Bubble Tea v2".
'   D9  how the port draws (tui-responsiveness.puml). DECIDED — the Executor:
'       "Rewrite the views in lipgloss". W1's tree, W6's step list and W9's
'       button row are lipgloss views; bubbles supplies tree, spinner and
'       text input, and has no form, radio, checkbox or button.
'   D13 starship, D14 the font (tui-responsiveness.puml). DECIDED — W11.
'   D6  when `run` shows the scope page. DECIDED — the Executor: "Every run,
'       Enter keeps root". Not chosen: first run only with a per-repo memory;
'       a row inside the form, which would have deleted W2's page loop.
'   D7  destructive confirms. DECIDED — the Executor: "Buttons, two keys to
'       destroy". Not chosen: a mnemonic that acts at once, which would make
'       `sbx rm --force` one key; keeping typed y/N; typing the sandbox name.
'   D10 the skip control. DECIDED — the Executor: "A focusable Skip button".
'       Not chosen: a control-key chord; no skip.
'   D17 `--yes` in a monorepo. DECIDED — the Executor: "Repo root, with a
'       line". W2's scope gate prints `scope: repo root`.
'   D18 the font archive. DECIDED — the Executor: "The .zip, 27 MB". Go's
'       standard library unpacks it and has no xz reader.
title PLANNED — two wizards, one step model:\na tree for the folder, a list for the work, a button for the answer

rectangle "proveo run" as RUNW <<host>> {
  component "1 · scope\na folder tree, root first" as SCOPE <<app>>
  component "2 · options\nthe form, now page 2/2" as OPTS <<app>>
  component "confirm\nonly when the sandbox changed" as CONF <<app>>
  component "starting\nlive step list" as START <<app>>
  component "Ctrl+C\nStay ↵ · Remove · Interrupt" as CC <<app>>
  component "finishing\nlive step list" as FIN <<app>>
  component "done\nthe prompt remembers" as RDONE <<host>>
}

rectangle "proveo init" as INITW <<host>> {
  component "1 · preflight\nevery check, with its mark" as PRE <<app>>
  component "2 · setup\nsays what Enter will run" as SETUP <<app>>
  component "3 · apply\nlive step list" as APPLY <<app>>
  component "4 · prompt\nicon, or empty box?" as GLYPH <<app>>
  component "5 · credentials\na named way to skip" as CRED <<app>>
  component "6 · operator" as OPER <<app>>
  component "7 · done\nready · later · next" as IDONE <<app>>
}

component "W2 · step chip + way back\n""Step{At, Of}""" as STEP <<app>>
component "W3 · two-tone key line" as HINT <<app>>
component "W6 · live step list\nelapsed · ceiling" as LIVE <<app>>
component "W9 · button row\nsafe default, red mnemonic" as BTN <<app>>
component "W11 · the prompt kit\nstarship · a Nerd Font if none" as KIT <<host>>
cloud "sbx 0.50.0 dashboard\nas recorded" as SBX <<cloud>>
cloud "starship 1.27 · Nerd Fonts 3.5\npinned, checksummed" as STAR <<cloud>>
component "go-fuzzyfinder\nthree call sites, three files" as FUZZY <<error>>

SCOPE ARROW_MAIN OPTS
OPTS ARROW_OPTIONAL CONF
OPTS ARROW_MAIN START
CONF ARROW_MAIN START
START ARROW_MAIN CC : the agent runs
CC ARROW_MAIN FIN
FIN ARROW_MAIN RDONE
PRE ARROW_MAIN SETUP
SETUP ARROW_MAIN APPLY
APPLY ARROW_MAIN GLYPH
GLYPH ARROW_MAIN CRED
CRED ARROW_MAIN OPER
OPER ARROW_MAIN IDONE
FUZZY ARROW_ERROR SCOPE : one of three replaced
STEP ARROW_OPTIONAL SCOPE
STEP ARROW_OPTIONAL PRE
HINT ARROW_OPTIONAL OPTS
LIVE ARROW_OPTIONAL START
LIVE ARROW_OPTIONAL APPLY
LIVE ARROW_OPTIONAL FIN
BTN ARROW_OPTIONAL CONF
BTN ARROW_OPTIONAL CC
KIT ARROW_OPTIONAL APPLY : two more steps
KIT ARROW_OPTIONAL GLYPH
KIT ARROW_OPTIONAL RDONE : the segment it shows
STAR ARROW_OPTIONAL KIT
SBX ARROW_OPTIONAL STEP : the 1/2 chip
SBX ARROW_OPTIONAL HINT : bold key, grey word
SBX ARROW_OPTIONAL BTN : No ↵ · Yes

note bottom of SCOPE
  **Root first, and marked.** The cursor starts
  on the repo root and a chip reads "default".
  Enter alone keeps today's answer; the line
  under the tree says where the agent starts.
end note

note bottom of FUZZY
  **It does not leave with the tree.** The tree
  replaces the scope picker only. The attach
  list and proveo-dev's multi-select keep it,
  and tcell with it, until they move too.
end note

note bottom of OPTS
  **Same rows, one more page behind it.** A
  ""Step{2, 2}"" form already draws its page and
  its way back. Gating and help text stay as
  wireframe.puml has them.
end note

note bottom of SETUP
  **Enter has consequences; name them.** The
  form lists what Enter will run, in order.
  The count follows "enter accept"; the e2e
  suite waits on that literal.
end note

note bottom of PRE
  **Prereqs, then diagnose.** Virtualisation is
  not an install prereq; ""sbx diagnose"" checks
  it once sbx exists. A fresh macOS host shows
  one row here.
end note

note bottom of CRED
  **Esc means three things in init today.** An
  error on setup, a skip here, a clean end on
  operator. ""s"" cannot be the skip key: it
  types into the focused field.
end note

note bottom of LIVE
  **One renderer, three phases.** Start, apply
  and teardown each show finished steps, the
  running step with its clock, and what is
  left. Plain output gets start and end lines.
end note

note bottom of BTN
  **The safe answer holds Enter.** A red bold
  letter inside the word is the key for the
  destructive one. Replacing still takes two
  keys, as typing y then Enter does.
end note

note bottom of GLYPH
  **Installed is not enabled.** A font file on
  disk does nothing until the terminal uses
  it, and proveo cannot ask the terminal. So
  it asks the operator and picks the preset.
end note

note bottom of KIT
  **Download only when none is there.** init
  fetches FiraCode Nerd Font when the host has
  no Nerd Font at install time. It never
  overwrites a starship.toml that exists.
end note

legend bottom
  **The proposals** — their order, slices and gates live in ""_spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml""
  ==
  **W1** the tree picker · **W2** the step model for run · **W3** two-tone key hints ·
  **W4** esc back, ctrl+c quit, a skip key (D10) · **W5** the on-enter region
  --
  **W6** the live step list for start and init's apply · **W7** init's preflight page ·
  **W8** init's result page · **W9** button confirmations (D7)
  ==
  **W10** the prompt segment and its verbs · **W11** the prompt kit: starship, and
  FiraCode Nerd Font when the host has none, installed by the same post-install as sbx
end legend
@enduml
